From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:58:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 209/225] cpufreq: sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq: fix of_node_put
 underflow on policy init

sprd_cpu_binning_parse() put info->cpufreq_np on every policy init even
though info_init() already balanced its reference and the node is kept
in info for later opp updates - refcount_t underflow splat per cluster.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq.c
index f31c444e2..6873b64a5 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq.c
@@ -540,9 +540,13 @@ static int sprd_cpu_binning_parse(struct sprd_cpufreq_info *info)
 	dev_dbg(info->pdev, "opp name after cpu bin parsed: %s\n",
 		clu->opp_name);
 
+	/*
+	 * Do not of_node_put(info->cpufreq_np) here (vendor code did):
+	 * info_init() already balanced its reference and the node stays
+	 * cached in info for later opp updates; the extra put underflows
+	 * the refcount on every policy init.
+	 */
 out:
-	of_node_put(info->cpufreq_np);
-
 	return ret;
 }
 
